## Tracker (raid 2026-10-28)
Imagine estimated ~20 files and a shared contract (the `## /gaze result` PR comment, read by attribution,
trace-pr-join, roar capture, detached-gaze polling). Blind-Spot showed a naive split leaves gaze writing notes
while verify-gate reads comments, so the order keeps a dual-write:
- 1299 landing push (criterion 3). Blocked-by: none.
- 1300 notes evidence for PR units, comment dual-written, review keyed by PR not bare branch name (criteria 2, 4; 1 notes half). Blocked-by: 1299.
- 1301 cut-over: comment becomes a pointer, readers move to notes, texts and STATE (criteria 1, 5). Blocked-by: 1300.
Open for the author, not blocking: review-heads retention (unbounded ref growth, flows memo §10).
Close after the integration review, not on the last child's merge.

## Context
Author ruling 2026-10-27 (ticket 1277 log, PR #1809): F1 = notes review + forge PR merge. Built so far
(1273-1281): notes review only for `branch:<name>` units; `scripts/forge.py` `get_forge` sends any numeric
review ref to GhForge, so F1 evidence is still PR comments. Author 2026-10-28: independence from the forge
comes first; review notes stay local, any push runs in the background, one sync at PR merge.

Measured on padme 2026-10-28: one notes round-trip to origin ~0.45 s, one `gh` API read ~0.5 s, a local
note read ~0 s. Today's notes path with a remote publishes synchronously with re-fetch read-back after each
gaze answer and verdict (`gaze_close.py`, `review_notes.py publish`), and `review_notes.py gate` syncs first.

## Design (default; the implementer may refine)
- Review of a PR number in a repository with `origin`: gaze and verify-gate write to `refs/notes/review`,
  keyed by the PR's head branch; no review evidence on the PR.
- Every review write is local. A push, if any, is best-effort in the background; never blocks, never
  read back. Readers (`gate`, `resolve`) try a fetch, and a failed fetch is reported, never read as "no review".
- At landing (`raid_land.py` / merge recipe), before `gh pr merge`: push `refs/notes/review` (and the
  review-heads) synchronously, never forced; a non-zero exit refuses the merge. Exit code suffices: a git push
  is atomic, unlike a forge API mutation, so no separate re-fetch read-back.
- Best-effort one-line PR comment pointing at the review (`review on notes: <id>, verdict <V>`) so the PR
  page is not blank; its failure is ignored (no forge dependency). Author may drop it.
- Web sessions stay outcome B (1277): readers and seats, entries leave by export/import.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] gaze on a PR number in a repo with `origin` writes its answer to `refs/notes/review`, not a PR comment, with no network call on the write path.
- [ ] verify-gate on a PR number reads gaze findings from notes and records its verdict in notes.
- [ ] Landing pushes `refs/notes/review` before the merge and refuses on a failed push; test covers the refusal.
- [ ] A failed background push or reader fetch never blocks a review and never reads as "no review"; tests cover both.
- [ ] Skill texts (gaze, verify-gate, merge, raid) and STATE describe one F1 evidence path; `make check` passes.
